            <div xml:id="d538">

                <pb facs="0675" n="555" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg555"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">815.00 Revolutions/3: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-04-18T21:00:00-06:00">April 18, 1931—9
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 10:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>59. My 58, April 18, 2 p.m. Following just received from American Vice Consul at
                    Ceiba: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Send warship immediately, American lives in danger.”</p></quote></p>
                <p>I approve and urge immediate action. Details follow by telegraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
